758
00:34:35.000 --> 00:34:36.340
He wants to be in the club.

759
00:34:36.340 --> 00:34:39.580
And Pam tells him it's a closed club.

760
00:34:40.340 --> 00:34:44.840
She's very direct and unapologetic.

761
00:34:44.840 --> 00:34:45.620
I'm sorry.

762
00:34:45.860 --> 00:34:47.240
This is a closed club.

763
00:34:47.520 --> 00:34:53.940
And Andy has a talking head where he says the Finer Things Club is the most exclusive club in the office.

764
00:34:53.940 --> 00:34:56.180
So it's naturally where he needs to be.

765
00:34:56.880 --> 00:34:59.180
Party planning committee is his backup.

766
00:34:59.760 --> 00:35:01.180
Kevin's band is his safety.

767
00:35:02.700 --> 00:35:04.980
Everything is like he's rushing a fraternity.

768
00:35:04.980 --> 00:35:06.500
It's so true.

769
00:35:06.940 --> 00:35:07.860
It's so true.

770
00:35:08.140 --> 00:35:11.260
Well, I'll have you know, we loved shooting these scenes.

771
00:35:11.480 --> 00:35:13.140
Me, Oscar, Paul.

772
00:35:13.380 --> 00:35:15.220
We were delighted by the storyline.

773
00:35:15.460 --> 00:35:19.760
We had the best time because this was a group of people that did not normally get to hang out.

774
00:35:19.920 --> 00:35:22.260
I did not have a lot of scenes with Oscar or Paul.

775
00:35:22.380 --> 00:35:24.040
So this was really cool.

776
00:35:24.220 --> 00:35:30.120
And I'll have you know that before the pandemic, we had a Finer Things Club reunion lunch.

777
00:35:30.120 --> 00:35:31.100
You did.

778
00:35:31.140 --> 00:35:33.680
I thought this was so, so sweet.

779
00:35:33.680 --> 00:35:37.060
When you told me you guys were all going to meet, I was like, that is adorable.

780
00:35:37.460 --> 00:35:38.400
Yeah, we met.

781
00:35:38.480 --> 00:35:41.160
We had lunch and we invited Ed.

782
00:35:41.420 --> 00:35:43.120
Oh, let Ed come.

783
00:35:44.580 --> 00:35:47.020
So the four of us had this amazing lunch.

784
00:35:47.140 --> 00:35:47.720
I took a picture.

785
00:35:47.860 --> 00:35:48.920
So I'll post it in the pod.

786
00:35:49.060 --> 00:35:50.220
That is so sweet.

787
00:35:50.340 --> 00:35:50.920
I'm very sad.

788
00:35:51.060 --> 00:35:53.900
I wasn't invited on the show or in real life.

789
00:35:53.900 --> 00:35:58.860
Well, I'll say we did not discuss any literature or art at our reunion lunch.

790
00:35:58.860 --> 00:36:01.700
We just chatted about our lives and our kids.

791
00:36:02.420 --> 00:36:06.240
Oh, well, now the guys have rolled up to the Utica branch.

792
00:36:06.420 --> 00:36:09.900
But Jenna, first, I want to talk to you about a deleted scene.

793
00:36:10.080 --> 00:36:12.100
You will not believe this scene.

794
00:36:12.440 --> 00:36:14.600
I had Sam pull this clip.

795
00:36:15.060 --> 00:36:19.260
Jim has called Pam from the road with Michael and Dwight.

796
00:36:19.260 --> 00:36:27.360
And Pam is kind of passive-aggressively giving Jim a little shade for seeing Karen.

797
00:36:27.780 --> 00:36:31.180
Oh, I don't even remember doing this scene.

798
00:36:31.360 --> 00:36:32.580
I couldn't believe it.

799
00:36:32.640 --> 00:36:34.620
It just doesn't even sound like Pam to me.

800
00:36:34.700 --> 00:36:37.160
And I think there's a reason it was deleted.

801
00:36:37.320 --> 00:36:39.080
But it's pretty delicious to listen to.

802
00:36:39.220 --> 00:36:40.140
Sam, can you play it?

803
00:36:41.160 --> 00:36:42.880
Wait, you're going along with this now?

804
00:36:43.080 --> 00:36:43.800
I have to.

805
00:36:44.320 --> 00:36:47.300
Pam, if I'm not there, someone's going to go to jail or die.

806
00:36:47.940 --> 00:36:48.460
Right.

807
00:36:48.920 --> 00:36:50.660
And you wouldn't be able to talk to Karen.

808
00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:53.100
Well, I promise you that has nothing to do with it.

809
00:36:53.340 --> 00:36:53.960
A little bit.

810
00:36:54.360 --> 00:36:57.100
Well, yeah, I don't want to see her get physically harmed, that's for sure.

811
00:36:57.280 --> 00:36:58.200
Because you love her?

812
00:36:58.360 --> 00:36:59.540
Because you love her very much?

813
00:36:59.600 --> 00:37:00.440
All right, I'm going to go now.

814
00:37:00.600 --> 00:37:01.740
Okay, have fun with your girlfriend.

815
00:37:02.340 --> 00:37:03.120
Okay, I will.

816
00:37:05.080 --> 00:37:09.700
I mean, Jenna, you're going to have fun with your little girlfriend?

817
00:37:10.040 --> 00:37:11.920
Oh my gosh, Pam is totally jealous.

818
00:37:12.500 --> 00:37:13.320
I don't know.

819
00:37:13.460 --> 00:37:14.560
Do you think she's really jealous?

820
00:37:14.560 --> 00:37:18.640
Yes, Pam also has a talking head where she's like, I was just kidding.

821
00:37:18.760 --> 00:37:19.400
We kid like that.

822
00:37:19.500 --> 00:37:21.060
And then she's like, okay, maybe I'm a little jealous.

823
00:37:21.440 --> 00:37:23.720
Wow, I don't even remember shooting that.

824
00:37:23.940 --> 00:37:24.140
Yeah.

825
00:37:24.280 --> 00:37:25.160
That's so crazy.

826
00:37:25.460 --> 00:37:27.040
You have to watch the deleted scenes.

827
00:37:27.260 --> 00:37:31.800
That does sound a little bit like me when I'm being passive aggressive.

828
00:37:33.100 --> 00:37:34.800
That was more Jenna than Pam.

829
00:37:35.000 --> 00:37:35.960
Maybe a little bit.

830
00:37:36.160 --> 00:37:41.300
I think it's good that they deleted it because I think I like instead, you know, that he comes

831
00:37:41.300 --> 00:37:43.540
back at the end of the day and, you know, I don't know.

832
00:37:43.620 --> 00:37:45.180
I don't want to see that side of Pam.

833
00:37:45.720 --> 00:37:49.120
Yeah, I just don't think we need that tension in the relationship.

834
00:37:49.120 --> 00:37:51.240
It doesn't need to be about that, you know?

835
00:37:51.480 --> 00:37:51.720
Yeah.

836
00:37:51.900 --> 00:37:56.340
I like it and we'll get to it that Jim and Karen are going to have a moment where they

837
00:37:56.340 --> 00:37:57.560
have to deal with their stuff.

838
00:37:57.560 --> 00:37:59.720
But I like that Pam is left out of it.

839
00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:00.580
Yeah, me too.

840
00:38:00.580 --> 00:38:05.540
So now the guys roll up to the Utica branch and Michael reveals their plan.

841
00:38:05.960 --> 00:38:10.200
They're going to pretend to be warehouse workers and they're going to silly string the whole

842
00:38:10.200 --> 00:38:10.720
place.

843
00:38:11.140 --> 00:38:16.540
Dwight adds that he might stab the security guy in the eye with a piece of jumbo chalk.

844
00:38:16.920 --> 00:38:20.160
And Jim is like, you're not stabbing anyone in the eye.

845
00:38:20.800 --> 00:38:21.740
Dwight's like, okay, fine.

846
00:38:21.840 --> 00:38:24.240
Maybe I'll just grind it up and blow it in his eyes.

847
00:38:24.840 --> 00:38:30.420
Yeah, he has a talking head that he says the eyes are the groin of the head.

848
00:38:30.580 --> 00:38:31.140
Yeah.

849
00:38:31.420 --> 00:38:33.920
So look out, eyeballs, if Dwight's around.

850
00:38:34.180 --> 00:38:35.740
I really love that line.

851
00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:36.840
I did too.

852
00:38:37.420 --> 00:38:41.880
Dwight and Michael leave and Jim is now on a walkie-talkie in the car.

853
00:38:42.120 --> 00:38:43.420
Well, and he sees Karen.

854
00:38:43.700 --> 00:38:44.680
He's like, oh my God, she's here.

855
00:38:44.760 --> 00:38:45.220
Go, go, go.

856
00:38:45.360 --> 00:38:48.940
And he leans the seat back trying to hide from Karen.

857
00:38:48.940 --> 00:38:49.600
Yeah.

858
00:38:49.820 --> 00:38:55.120
But in the meantime, through the walkie-talkie, we only hear it, which I personally think

859
00:38:55.120 --> 00:38:56.400
is so freaking funny.

860
00:38:56.840 --> 00:38:59.980
Michael and Dwight decide to steal the industrial copier.

861
00:39:00.180 --> 00:39:03.420
Then you hear a very loud crashing noise.

862
00:39:03.780 --> 00:39:08.180
And then you start to hear Michael talking about his hip.

863
00:39:08.640 --> 00:39:10.540
He's saying, Jim, save us.

864
00:39:11.140 --> 00:39:15.720
He's saying, Jim, if this is my last moment, please tell me you'll take over the Dundies.

865
00:39:16.460 --> 00:39:19.180
It's so, so amazing.

866
00:39:19.700 --> 00:39:21.280
And Jenna, you're so right.

867
00:39:21.440 --> 00:39:23.280
It was better over the walkie-talkie.

868
00:39:23.360 --> 00:39:28.100
There's a deleted scene in the stairwell where Michael is pinned by the copier.

869
00:39:28.260 --> 00:39:29.820
And there's silly string everywhere.

870
00:39:30.100 --> 00:39:31.680
And the security guards have come.

871
00:39:31.840 --> 00:39:34.400
And it just plays funnier over the walkie-talkie.

872
00:39:34.480 --> 00:39:35.400
It really does.

873
00:39:35.400 --> 00:39:37.660
So I was really glad that they made that choice.

874
00:39:38.120 --> 00:39:40.120
I have a fan catch for this moment.

875
00:39:40.380 --> 00:39:40.720
Okay.

876
00:39:41.100 --> 00:39:45.540
When the guys were driving in the car, it was very clear that there was just Michael,

877
00:39:45.760 --> 00:39:47.620
Jim, and then Dwight in the back seat.

878
00:39:48.140 --> 00:39:53.340
But now, all of a sudden, we have a camera operator in the car with Jim.

879
00:39:53.620 --> 00:39:53.800
Yeah.

880
00:39:53.940 --> 00:39:55.140
And Jim is like, get down.

881
00:39:55.260 --> 00:39:55.880
What are you doing?

882
00:39:56.060 --> 00:39:56.360
You know?

883
00:39:56.560 --> 00:39:57.900
Where did this guy come from?

884
00:39:58.140 --> 00:40:02.220
And also, when they're on the side of the road, there was clearly a camera operator on

885
00:40:02.220 --> 00:40:03.140
the side of the road with them.

886
00:40:03.140 --> 00:40:08.180
So I have made up a story in my head that the camera operators followed them in another

887
00:40:08.180 --> 00:40:10.600
vehicle to document this moment.

888
00:40:10.900 --> 00:40:12.560
They had a huge budget.

889
00:40:12.840 --> 00:40:19.100
They put lipstick cameras in the car, rigged the car, then followed the car with a second

890
00:40:19.100 --> 00:40:20.360
set of handheld cameras.

891
00:40:20.600 --> 00:40:22.760
This PBS went all out.

892
00:40:22.900 --> 00:40:23.580
They really did.

893
00:40:23.800 --> 00:40:26.380
Well, they knew that this was going to be a good moment.

894
00:40:26.800 --> 00:40:27.160
Yeah.

895
00:40:27.160 --> 00:40:34.980
We had a fan question from Arisbeth Cruz, Zufan Gerard, Colby Shannon, and Caro B.

896
00:40:35.300 --> 00:40:39.240
Were Jim, Michael, and Dwight actually talking through walkie-talkies?

897
00:40:39.820 --> 00:40:40.700
Yes, they were.

898
00:40:40.960 --> 00:40:46.840
And I don't know if this was in the bloopers, Angela, but John was laughing so hard at what

899
00:40:46.840 --> 00:40:47.740
he was listening to.

900
00:40:48.020 --> 00:40:51.860
I remember him telling me stories, wait until you see this scene.

901
00:40:52.060 --> 00:40:55.140
These guys were so funny over the walkie-talkie.

902
00:40:55.140 --> 00:40:59.900
I loved when Jim kept saying, stop saying my name.

903
00:41:00.500 --> 00:41:01.180
Yes.

904
00:41:03.710 --> 00:41:08.510
Well, Karen spots Jim in the car and she walks over.

905
00:41:08.910 --> 00:41:10.390
So embarrassing.

906
00:41:10.830 --> 00:41:15.050
But then it leads into this amazing scene.

907
00:41:15.570 --> 00:41:18.630
She's got the three of them on a couch in her office.

908
00:41:18.630 --> 00:41:23.890
It 100% looks like three kids who've been called to the principal's office.

909
00:41:24.270 --> 00:41:24.690
Mm-hmm.

910
00:41:25.050 --> 00:41:26.610
Well, Karen is loving this.

911
00:41:26.610 --> 00:41:31.090
I mean, there's a whole talking head where she says, I cried for weeks over that guy.

912
00:41:31.250 --> 00:41:33.970
So yeah, it felt pretty good seeing him in this situation.

913
00:41:35.030 --> 00:41:37.990
The only person still wearing his mustache now is Dwight.

914
00:41:38.390 --> 00:41:40.290
Michael is defending his behavior.

915
00:41:40.530 --> 00:41:44.430
He is saying that he cares enough to fight for his employees.

916
00:41:44.430 --> 00:41:51.990
And if Stanley comes to Utica and she hurts one hair on his head, he will burn Utica to the ground.

917
00:41:52.690 --> 00:41:52.890
Yeah.

918
00:41:53.170 --> 00:41:57.590
Dwight and Michael both say they will burn Utica to the ground.

919
00:41:58.050 --> 00:41:58.690
Insane.

920
00:41:59.150 --> 00:42:01.750
So Karen sends Michael and Dwight away.

921
00:42:01.950 --> 00:42:04.130
She says, Jim, will you stay a moment?

922
00:42:04.650 --> 00:42:04.890
Ooh.

923
00:42:05.270 --> 00:42:05.430
Ooh.

924
00:42:05.430 --> 00:42:07.170
The principal kept one.

925
00:42:07.490 --> 00:42:08.550
Let the other two go.

926
00:42:08.850 --> 00:42:10.490
Well, now it's going to get personal.

927
00:42:10.810 --> 00:42:12.530
Oh, this is so cringy.

928
00:42:12.730 --> 00:42:16.250
She says, Jim, if you wanted to see me, you could have just called.

929
00:42:16.790 --> 00:42:18.970
And Jim's like, oh, no, I didn't want to see you.

930
00:42:19.470 --> 00:42:19.750
Oh.

931
00:42:20.170 --> 00:42:20.570
Oh.

932
00:42:21.050 --> 00:42:28.730
And he's like, not that I'm not happy that, you know, to see you, but I know I was I was basically just here for the copier because I'm, you know,

933
00:42:29.130 --> 00:42:30.750
with Pam and things are going well.

934
00:42:30.950 --> 00:42:31.930
And, you know, we're good.

935
00:42:32.030 --> 00:42:38.290
And she's like, oh, I'm so glad to hear that things are going so well for you.

936
00:42:39.110 --> 00:42:39.990
Oh, yeah.

937
00:42:41.230 --> 00:42:45.490
Angela, we had a fan catch for this scene from Rachel Watkins.

938
00:42:45.490 --> 00:42:55.390
At 17 minutes, 27 seconds, as Karen and Jim are having their one-on-one, Karen has a photo of Hillary Clinton on her bookshelf.

939
00:42:55.810 --> 00:43:04.830
Rachel is wondering if this is a nod to Leslie Knope having framed photos of Hillary Clinton in her office for Parks and Recreation.

940
00:43:05.170 --> 00:43:06.410
You know what, Rachel?

941
00:43:06.610 --> 00:43:07.470
I don't know.

942
00:43:07.670 --> 00:43:09.050
But what a great catch.

943
00:43:09.530 --> 00:43:09.890
Yeah.

944
00:43:10.170 --> 00:43:11.630
I didn't catch that.

945
00:43:11.830 --> 00:43:13.290
I zoomed in on it.

946
00:43:13.290 --> 00:43:17.610
But speaking of Parks and Recreation, Angela, we had another fan question.

947
00:43:17.790 --> 00:43:19.190
A bunch of people wrote in.

948
00:43:19.290 --> 00:43:22.690
They said, how did you get Rashida Jones back for this?

949
00:43:22.810 --> 00:43:24.930
Wasn't she on Parks and Recreation at the time?

950
00:43:25.110 --> 00:43:25.930
She was.

951
00:43:26.110 --> 00:43:33.610
But you might remember that Parks and Rec was created by Mike Schur, who was one of the office writers.

952
00:43:33.870 --> 00:43:40.430
And so our production office just called over to their production office and they were able to clear her for one day of work.

953
00:43:40.430 --> 00:43:46.650
So she came and did this one shooting day at these offices for Utica, but we didn't get to see her.

954
00:43:46.830 --> 00:43:51.030
We did not get to have a reunion with her at all because she was on location.

955
00:43:51.390 --> 00:43:52.130
I know.

956
00:43:52.430 --> 00:43:55.170
I just thought she crushed these scenes.

957
00:43:55.410 --> 00:43:56.810
She was so perfect in them.

958
00:43:57.130 --> 00:44:02.810
Well, Jenna, there's a whole lot happening back at Dunder Mifflin because the Finer Things Club is trying to have their meeting.

959
00:44:02.970 --> 00:44:04.690
You know, they had to hang a sign.

960
00:44:04.690 --> 00:44:10.250
You have to think someone hangs a sign because events have happened, right?

961
00:44:10.590 --> 00:44:11.010
Yes.

962
00:44:11.170 --> 00:44:12.790
And the solution is a sign.

963
00:44:12.930 --> 00:44:15.790
So they have made a sign at 12 minutes, 49 seconds.

964
00:44:15.910 --> 00:44:16.530
You can catch it.

965
00:44:16.650 --> 00:44:19.030
It says, Finer Things Club in progress.

966
00:44:19.610 --> 00:44:21.090
Please be respectful.

967
00:44:21.770 --> 00:44:23.410
And Kevin comes in.

968
00:44:23.570 --> 00:44:25.330
He's trying to get something out of the vending machine.

969
00:44:25.330 --> 00:44:27.090
He's banging it back and forth.

970
00:44:27.270 --> 00:44:29.530
His butt is like right up against your chair.

971
00:44:29.530 --> 00:44:39.710
And my absolute favorite moment of all of the Finer Things Club meetings is Phyllis and that dang microwave.

972
00:44:40.230 --> 00:44:43.090
How many buttons is she hitting?

973
00:44:43.630 --> 00:44:45.030
So many buttons.

974
00:44:45.290 --> 00:44:46.450
So many buttons.

975
00:44:46.630 --> 00:44:50.350
And Oscar, he is so fantastic.

976
00:44:50.350 --> 00:44:57.590
The way he lets it amp up and start to bug him as he's trying to form his thought about his book sharing, right?

977
00:44:57.590 --> 00:44:59.390
He wants to tell you guys about this book.

978
00:44:59.650 --> 00:45:01.510
Beep, beep, beep, beep, beep.

979
00:45:01.670 --> 00:45:05.590
And then finally he just snaps and he's like, what are you microwaving?

980
00:45:06.490 --> 00:45:10.810
And Phyllis says popcorn with her St. Louis accent.

981
00:45:11.230 --> 00:45:13.710
We had a lot of people write in and catch that.

982
00:45:14.490 --> 00:45:16.670
1349, you hear a solid popcorn.

983
00:45:17.470 --> 00:45:18.810
This is me though, Jenna.

984
00:45:19.050 --> 00:45:19.930
I am Oscar.

985
00:45:20.350 --> 00:45:24.590
If you want to drive me crazy, have some beeping somewhere.

986
00:45:25.070 --> 00:45:26.670
Something beeping makes me nuts.

987
00:45:26.670 --> 00:45:31.850
You know, I have to turn off the beeping on my washer dryer.

988
00:45:32.710 --> 00:45:35.370
I don't need that to keep going off.

989
00:45:35.550 --> 00:45:37.470
I know I put the laundry in.

990
00:45:37.610 --> 00:45:40.210
I know I'll take the laundry out eventually.

991
00:45:40.530 --> 00:45:41.770
I'll get to it.

992
00:45:41.870 --> 00:45:48.030
I don't need you alarming me to my dry laundry for the next 15 minutes off and on.

993
00:45:48.270 --> 00:45:51.050
I don't get why everything has to beep so much.

994
00:45:51.270 --> 00:45:52.770
The refrigerator beeps.

995
00:45:53.130 --> 00:45:54.490
The dishwasher beeps.

996
00:45:54.630 --> 00:45:55.550
The microwave beeps.

997
00:45:55.550 --> 00:45:57.390
My coffee maker beeps.

998
00:45:57.670 --> 00:46:00.990
It beeps when it's done and then it beeps when it turns itself off.

999
00:46:01.170 --> 00:46:02.110
So much beeping.

1000
00:46:02.650 --> 00:46:04.230
Can we tone it down on the beeping?

1001
00:46:04.890 --> 00:46:05.870
Appliance people?

1002
00:46:06.290 --> 00:46:08.270
Not everything needs an alarm.

1003
00:46:09.630 --> 00:46:10.430
You know?

1004
00:46:11.390 --> 00:46:13.510
This is, we feel strongly about this.

